{"name":"Galway Bay","hex":"#95a7a4","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Galway Bay","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A bay off the west coast of Ireland, between the counties of Galway and Clare."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Galway_Bay"}],"entries":[{"title":"Galway Bay","blocks":[{"text":"Galway Bay is a bay on the west coast of Ireland, between County Galway in the province of Connacht to the north and the Burren in County Clare in the province of Munster to the south; Galway city is on the northeast side. The bay is about 50 kilometres (30 mi) long and from 10 kilometres (6 mi) to 30 kilometres (20 mi) in breadth. The Aran Islands are to the west across the entrance and there are numerous small islands within the bay. To the west of Galway, the rocks are granite but to the south they are limestone."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/Galway_Bay_and_Co._Clare_%28506274%29_%2826553934032%29.jpg/330px-Galway_Bay_and_Co._Clare_%28506274%29_%2826553934032%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Galway_Bay","wikidata":"Q1127599"},{"title":"Galway Bay (song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Galway Bay\" is the name of at least three different songs named after Galway Bay in the west of Ireland."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Galway_Bay_(song)","wikidata":"Q11971467"},{"title":"Galway","blocks":[{"text":"Galway is a city in County Galway. It lies on the River Corrib between Lough Corrib and Galway Bay. It is the most populous settlement in the province of Connacht, the fifth most populous city on the island of Ireland and the fourth most populous in the Republic of Ireland, with a population at the 2022 census of 85,910."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/Galway_cathedral.jpg/330px-Galway_cathedral.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Galway","wikidata":"Q129610"},{"title":"Bay","blocks":[{"text":"A bay is a recessed, coastal body of water that directly connects to a larger main body of water, such as an ocean, a lake, or another bay. A large bay is usually called a gulf, sea, sound, or bight. A cove is a small, circular bay with a narrow entrance. A fjord is an elongated bay formed by glacial action.\nThe term embayment is also used for related features, such as extinct bays or freshwater environments."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/Aerial_photograph_of_Langness_and_the_bay_at_Castletown_13_February_2014_-_geograph.org.uk_-_3847162.jpg/330px-Aerial_photograph_of_Langness_and_the_bay_at_Castletown_13_February_2014_-_geograph.org.uk_-_3847162.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bay","wikidata":"Q39594"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/Claddagh_Memorial_Galway_Bay.jpg/330px-Claddagh_Memorial_Galway_Bay.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/Claddagh_Memorial_Galway_Bay.jpg/330px-Claddagh_Memorial_Galway_Bay.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Cladagh Memorial opposite St Mary's Church, the Claddagh, Galway","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACladdagh_Memorial_Galway_Bay.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Galway_Bay_from_Salthill.jpg/120px-Galway_Bay_from_Salthill.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Galway_Bay_from_Salthill.jpg/250px-Galway_Bay_from_Salthill.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Galway_Bay_from_Salt